SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"The Bank of Russia increases the key rate by 100 b.p. to 9.50% p.a.","publisher":"Bank of Russia","publication_date":"2022-02-11","url":"https://www.cbr.ru/eng/press/pr/?file=11022022_133000Key_eng.htm","claim":"The Bank of Russia raised the key rate because inflation was above forecast and demand was outpacing output capacity.","locator":"statement body, lines 46-53","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary central-bank press release with clear dated policy action and rationale.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"target-period 2022","ruler_attribution":"Indirect but material. The Bank of Russia is operationally independent, yet it was acting within Putin's wartime state environment.","contrary_evidence":["The wider economy still faced sanctions and later recession pressures."],"lenses":["5B.3","5B.7","5B.9"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Bank of Russia increases the key rate to 20% p.a.","publisher":"Bank of Russia","publication_date":"2022-02-28","url":"https://www.cbr.ru/eng/press/pr/?file=28022022_094500key_eng.htm","claim":"The Bank of Russia hiked the key rate to 20% to support financial and price stability and protect household savings from depreciation.","locator":"statement body, lines 46-46","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary policy announcement with explicit rationale and immediate macro-stabilization intent.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"target-period 2022","ruler_attribution":"Indirect but material through the regime's monetary authority; the action occurred under Putin's invasion and sanctions shock.","contrary_evidence":["The need for an emergency hike itself indicates severe instability after the invasion and sanctions."],"lenses":["5B.3","5B.9"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"The Bank of Russia keeps the key rate at 20% p.a.","publisher":"Bank of Russia","publication_date":"2022-03-18","url":"https://www.cbr.ru/eng/press/pr/?file=18032022_133000key_eng.htm","claim":"The central bank said the 28 February hike and capital controls helped support stable functioning of the financial system, while it kept the key rate at 20%.","locator":"statement body, lines 51-51","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary central-bank statement describing crisis measures and their stated effect.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"target-period 2022","ruler_attribution":"Indirect but material; the bank acted under war-induced financial stress, not as a neutral peacetime actor.","contrary_evidence":["The same release says external conditions had changed drastically and threatened financial stability."],"lenses":["5B.3","5B.9"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"The Bank of Russia cuts the key rate by 300 b.p. to 14.00% p.a.","publisher":"Bank of Russia","publication_date":"2022-04-29","url":"https://www.cbr.ru/eng/press/pr/?file=29042022_133000Key_eng.htm","claim":"The bank cut the rate to 14%, projected 2022 inflation at 18.0-23.0%, and forecast GDP to fall 8.0-10.0% in 2022.","locator":"statement body, lines 49-61","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary macro-policy release with specific forecasts and policy response.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"target-period 2022","ruler_attribution":"Indirect but material via the central bank's wartime stabilization role under Putin's state.","contrary_evidence":["The bank still expected a severe contraction and sustained inflation."],"lenses":["5B.3","5B.9","5B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Monetary Policy Guidelines for 2022-2024","publisher":"Bank of Russia","publication_date":"2021-11-26","url":"https://www.cbr.ru/eng/about_br/publ/ondkp/on_2022_2024/","claim":"The Bank of Russia stated that price stability close to 4% is its main goal and that forecast-based decisions and transparency are core monetary-policy principles.","locator":"Goals and principles section, lines 10-30","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary policy framework document describing stated objectives and tools.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"pre-2022 baseline for target-period monetary policy","ruler_attribution":"Indirect context only; this is the framework Putin governed through, not a discrete ruler action in 2022.","contrary_evidence":["The framework does not itself prove competent execution in 2022."],"lenses":["5B.3","5B.7"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Putin tips central bank chief Nabiullina for third term to ensure economic stability","publisher":"Reuters via Investing.com","publication_date":"2022-03-18","url":"https://www.investing.com/news/economy/russias-putin-proposes-to-reappoint-central-bank-chief-nabiullina-2787264","claim":"Putin proposed reappointing Elvira Nabiullina for another term, explicitly framing the move as a bid to preserve macroeconomic stability.","locator":"headline and lede","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters reporting on a dated personnel decision; syndicated on Investing.com but the claim is specific and contemporaneous.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"target-period 2022","ruler_attribution":"Direct. This is a Putin-driven appointment signal about who would manage macro policy.","contrary_evidence":["Nabiullina still operated within a coercive wartime environment and could not set external policy conditions."],"lenses":["5B.2","5B.3","5B.7"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Putin orders new budget rules to boost Russia's growth","publisher":"Reuters via Investing.com","publication_date":"2022-06-07","url":"https://www.investing.com/news/economy/putin-orders-new-budget-rules-to-boost-russias-growth-2834324","claim":"Putin ordered new budget rules to support growth and said the rules should ensure stability of public finances and raise growth rates.","locator":"headline and lines 420-424","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters reporting on a specific Kremlin-directed policy instruction; clear ruler attribution and date.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"target-period 2022","ruler_attribution":"Direct. Putin personally ordered the budget-rule work.","contrary_evidence":["The same report notes Russia had suspended its prior budget rule and faced sanctions-driven reserve constraints."],"lenses":["5B.1","5B.3","5B.6","5B.7","5B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Russia to restrict budget data in response to Western sanctions","publisher":"Reuters via Investing.com","publication_date":"2022-06-14","url":"https://www.investing.com/news/economic-indicators/russia-to-restrict-budget-data-in-response-to-western-sanctions-2836927","claim":"Russia's finance ministry said it would partially restrict public budget-spending information in response to sanctions; the report also said Putin had pledged fresh social payments and that the National Wealth Fund would support key state enterprises.","locator":"lines 405-412","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters reporting on government and finance-ministry actions with direct policy detail.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"target-period 2022","ruler_attribution":"Direct for the social-payment pledge and broader fiscal direction; indirect for the finance-ministry disclosure restriction.","contrary_evidence":["Restricting budget data reduces transparency and can obscure who benefits from spending."],"lenses":["5B.1","5B.5","5B.7","5B.8","5B.9"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Russia increases its emergency spending fund by $4.6b","publisher":"The Straits Times / Reuters","publication_date":"2022-04-10","url":"https://www.straitstimes.com/world/europe/russia-increases-its-emergency-spending-fund-by-46b","claim":"Russia increased its emergency spending fund to ensure economic stability under sanctions and had already pledged more than 1 trillion roubles in anti-crisis support to businesses, social payments, and families with children.","locator":"lines 57-65","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters report republished by a major outlet; the claim is specific and dated, with direct policy content.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"target-period 2022","ruler_attribution":"Direct for the government's emergency fiscal response under Putin's authority.","contrary_evidence":["The same report says sanctions cut Russia off from the global financial system and supply channels."],"lenses":["5B.1","5B.6","5B.8","5B.9","5B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Russia's Putin calls for pension hike above inflation rate","publisher":"Euronews / Reuters","publication_date":"2022-01-12","url":"https://www.euronews.com/next/2022/01/12/russia-economy-pensions","claim":"Putin called for an 8.6% pension increase above inflation and had previously ordered one-off social payments and public-sector salary hikes worth at least 500 billion roubles.","locator":"lines 660-662","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters reporting on a clear Putin-directed social-spending choice, republished by Euronews.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"target-period 2022","ruler_attribution":"Direct. Putin personally directed the pension and social-payment policy.","contrary_evidence":["Analysts said the hikes could further fuel inflation."],"lenses":["5B.1","5B.8","5B.9"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Putin orders benefit payments for people arriving in Russia from Ukraine","publisher":"Reuters via Investing.com","publication_date":"2022-08-27","url":"https://www.investing.com/news/world-news/putin-orders-benefit-payments-for-people-arriving-in-russia-from-ukraine-2881261","claim":"Putin signed a decree establishing monthly pension payments and other benefits for people forced to leave Ukrainian territory for Russia.","locator":"lines 420-420","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters report on a dated decree with precise benefit terms and direct ruler action.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"target-period 2022","ruler_attribution":"Direct. This was a Putin-signed benefits decree.","contrary_evidence":["The policy is narrow and conflict-linked rather than broad-based prosperity policy."],"lenses":["5B.8","5B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Putin says Russia will post budget surplus this year, GDP to decline 'around 2%'","publisher":"Euronews / Reuters","publication_date":"2022-09-08","url":"https://www.euronews.com/2022/09/08/russia-economy-putin-forum","claim":"Putin said Russia would post a budget surplus in 2022 and forecast GDP would fall around 2%, a milder contraction than earlier expected.","locator":"lines 603-604","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters coverage of Putin's public economic forecast and budget claim, republished by Euronews.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"target-period 2022","ruler_attribution":"Direct. The claim is Putin's own public economic assessment.","contrary_evidence":["His optimism was more upbeat than the economy ministry and major banks, and it rested partly on energy-revenue windfalls."],"lenses":["5B.9","5B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Russia's 2022 economic fall seen in lower incomes, slumping consumer demand","publisher":"Reuters via Investing.com","publication_date":"2023-02-08","url":"https://www.investing.com/news/economy/russias-2022-economic-fall-seen-in-lower-incomes-slumping-consumer-demand-2998520","claim":"Russian consumer demand contracted at its fastest pace in seven years in 2022, real disposable incomes fell 1%, and retail sales slumped 6.7%.","locator":"lines 406-414","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters reporting on Rosstat data with specific household and demand indicators for 2022.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"retrospective evidence for the 2022 target year","ruler_attribution":"Indirect but material; these are economy-wide outcomes under Putin's wartime policy environment.","contrary_evidence":["Unemployment stayed at a record low, showing some labor-market resilience."],"lenses":["5B.8","5B.9","5B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Russian unemployment rate hits record low, economic data paints mixed picture","publisher":"Reuters via Investing.com","publication_date":"2022-09-28","url":"https://www.investing.com/news/economy/russian-unemployment-rate-hits-record-low-economic-data-paints-mixed-picture-2901110","claim":"Russia's unemployment fell to a record low 3.8%, but real wages fell 3.2% year on year in July and car production dropped 69%.","locator":"lines 427-439","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters report on Rosstat data with concrete labor-market and output figures.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"target-period 2022","ruler_attribution":"Indirect but material; the mixed labor-market result came under Putin's sanctions-era policy mix and mobilization shock.","contrary_evidence":["Low unemployment partly reflected labor shortages after mobilization and emigration, not broad prosperity."],"lenses":["5B.9","5B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"IMF Staff Statement on the Economic Impact of War in Ukraine","publisher":"IMF","publication_date":"2022-03-05","url":"https://www.imf.org/en/news/articles/2022/03/05/pr2261-imf-staff-statement-on-the-economic-impact-of-war-in-ukraine","claim":"The IMF said sanctions on the Russian Central Bank would severely restrict access to reserves, disrupt cross-border transactions, and that fiscal policy should support the most vulnerable households.","locator":"lines 266-272","source_type":"IGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary IMF statement issued immediately after the invasion with direct macro-financial assessment.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"target-period 2022","ruler_attribution":"Indirect but strong. The consequences flowed from Putin's invasion and the regime's response environment.","contrary_evidence":["The IMF was describing macro damage and policy needs, not praising Russian performance."],"lenses":["5B.3","5B.9","5B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"War Dims Global Economic Outlook as Inflation Accelerates","publisher":"IMF Blog","publication_date":"2022-04-19","url":"https://www.imf.org/en/blogs/articles/2022/04/19/blog-weo-war-dims-global-economic-outlook-as-inflation-accelerates","claim":"The IMF projected steep contractions for Russia and said the war and sanctions were increasing inflation and hurting lower-income households through food and fuel prices.","locator":"lines 45-50 and 61-64","source_type":"IGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official IMF analysis with explicit Russia-specific macro projections and distributional effects.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"target-period 2022","ruler_attribution":"Indirect but strong. The forecast explicitly ties Russia's contraction to Putin's war and sanctions.","contrary_evidence":["The same piece notes some commodity exporters benefited from higher energy and food prices."],"lenses":["5B.8","5B.9","5B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"WEO Update July 2022 Press Briefing Transcript","publisher":"IMF","publication_date":"2022-07-26","url":"https://www.imf.org/en/news/articles/2022/07/27/tr072622-weo-uptate-july-22-press-briefing-transcript","claim":"The IMF said Russia's domestic economy had been doing fairly well because emergency financial and monetary measures helped stabilize the financial sector, even though the projected 2022 contraction was still 6%.","locator":"lines 353-355 and 443-446","source_type":"IGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official IMF transcript with Russia-specific forecast revision and explanation of short-run stabilization.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"target-period 2022","ruler_attribution":"Indirect but material. The stabilization reflects the regime's macro response after Putin's invasion.","contrary_evidence":["The same transcript still describes a severe recession and worsening 2023 outlook."],"lenses":["5B.3","5B.9","5B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Financial Stability Review, May 2022","publisher":"ECB","publication_date":"2022-05-01","url":"https://www.ecb.europa.eu/press/financial-stability-publications/fsr/html/ecb.fsr202205~f207f46ea0.en.html","claim":"The ECB said sanctions had significantly isolated Russia's economy and were reflected in a sharp downgrade of its growth outlook and higher inflation expectations.","locator":"lines 807-807","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary central-bank analysis from a major international institution with explicit Russia assessment.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"target-period 2022","ruler_attribution":"Indirect macro context tied to Putin's invasion and the sanctions response.","contrary_evidence":["This is external analysis, not a Russian policy document."],"lenses":["5B.9","5B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"OECD Economic Outlook, Interim Report March 2022","publisher":"OECD","publication_date":"2022-03-17","url":"https://www.oecd.org/en/publications/oecd-economic-outlook/volume-2022/issue-2_4181d61b-en/full-report.html","claim":"The OECD said sanctions cut Russia off from foreign capital and reserves, the ruble depreciated sharply, the policy rate rose to 20%, and the downturn in Russia could be larger than after Crimea.","locator":"lines 3855-3859 and 3995-3996","source_type":"IGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary OECD analysis with explicit Russia-specific macro and financial-system effects.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"target-period 2022","ruler_attribution":"Indirect but strong. The report links these effects to Putin's invasion and the sanctions it triggered.","contrary_evidence":["Russia had some energy-revenue cushion and many domestic effects depended on sanctions intensity."],"lenses":["5B.3","5B.9","5B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Russia: Freedom in the World 2022 Country Report","publisher":"Freedom House","publication_date":"2022-02-24","url":"https://freedomhouse.org/country/russia/freedom-world/2022","claim":"Freedom House described Putin's system as centralized and corrupt, with elites receiving government contracts and protection in return for loyalty, and said the Kremlin manipulates elections and suppresses dissent.","locator":"overview and C2 section, lines 80-82 and 151-152","source_type":"NGO","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Major rights-monitoring assessment with clear Russia-wide institutional and corruption findings.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"2021-2022 baseline for the 2022 ruler-period","ruler_attribution":"Direct and indirect. The report ties corruption and patronage to Putin's personalist system.","contrary_evidence":["The report also notes that the regime maintains formal institutions and elections, albeit heavily manipulated."],"lenses":["5B.1","5B.4","5B.5","5B.7","5B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Russia: Nations in Transit 2022 Country Report","publisher":"Freedom House","publication_date":"2022-04-12","url":"https://freedomhouse.org/country/russia/nations-transit/2022","claim":"Freedom House said corruption among Russian elites is omnipresent, that access to officials' financial information was constrained by presidential decree, and that anti-corruption rules were being used to tighten control rather than increase oversight.","locator":"corruption section, lines 292-296","source_type":"NGO","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Detailed country report from a major democracy monitor with specific corruption and transparency findings.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"2021-2022 baseline for the 2022 ruler-period","ruler_attribution":"Direct and indirect. The report describes presidentially ordered transparency constraints and elite corruption under Putin.","contrary_evidence":["Russia also retained formal anti-corruption plans and some prosecutions, but the report says these were selective and politically useful."],"lenses":["5B.4","5B.5","5B.7","5B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Treasury Sanctions Russians Bankrolling Putin and Russia-Backed Influence Actors","publisher":"U.S. Department of the Treasury","publication_date":"2022-03-03","url":"https://home.treasury.gov/news/press-releases/jy0628","claim":"Treasury said Russian elites and family members were providing direct and indirect support to Putin's government and war, and that sanctions targeted disinformation outlets and defense enterprises.","locator":"press release body, lines 614-617","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary sanctions release from a major government source with specific designated-network claims.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"target-period 2022","ruler_attribution":"Indirect. This is external corroboration of Putin-linked elite networks rather than a Russian policy act.","contrary_evidence":["It reflects foreign sanctions action, not a domestic reform or welfare policy."],"lenses":["5B.5","5B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Russian Elites, Proxies, and Oligarchs Task Force Joint Statement","publisher":"U.S. Department of the Treasury","publication_date":"2022-06-29","url":"https://home.treasury.gov/news/press-releases/jy0839","claim":"The REPO task force said it had immobilized about $300 billion in Russian Central Bank assets and blocked or frozen more than $30 billion in sanctioned Russian assets.","locator":"joint statement body, lines 604-609","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary multinational sanctions statement with concrete figures.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"target-period 2022","ruler_attribution":"Indirect macro constraint from the sanctions environment created by Putin's invasion.","contrary_evidence":["These are foreign countermeasures, not evidence of Putin's economic stewardship by themselves."],"lenses":["5B.5","5B.9","5B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"World Bank Group Statement on Russia and Belarus","publisher":"World Bank Group","publication_date":"2022-03-02","url":"https://www.worldbank.org/en/news/statement/2022/03/02/world-bank-group-statement-on-russia-and-belarus","claim":"The World Bank said it stopped all its programs in Russia and Belarus immediately after the invasion.","locator":"statement body","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary institution statement describing a direct institutional response to the invasion.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"target-period 2022","ruler_attribution":"Indirect consequence of Putin's invasion and the resulting isolation of Russia.","contrary_evidence":["This is an external institutional response, not a domestic policy choice."],"lenses":["5B.9","5B.10"]}

Search ledger:
- Candidates found: about 60
- Documents opened: about 34
- Duplicates / near-duplicates removed: about 18
- Irrelevant or out-of-period: about 10
- Inaccessible or partial: about 6
- Accepted distinct URLs: 24

Material gaps:
- Direct Russian primary documents on 2022 budget execution, spending composition, and import-substitution policy are still thin.
- Better direct evidence on the economic team beyond Nabiullina, especially Siluanov, Reshetnikov, and who actually shaped crisis policy.
- Stronger distributional evidence is still needed on regional inequality, household welfare, and how much support reached ordinary households versus regime-linked firms.
- More direct evidence on whether emergency spending and industrial support broadened opportunity or mostly preserved loyalty networks.

Next best queries:
1. Search Russian-language primary sources for `бюджетное правило 2022`, `антикризисная поддержка`, `импортозамещение`, `медианная заработная плата 2022`, and `уровень бедности 2022`.
2. Pull direct Ministry of Finance, CBR, and Rosstat releases on 2022 budget execution, inflation, wages, poverty, and regional disparities.
3. Search investigative and scholarly work on sanctions evasion, state contracts, and which firms benefited from import substitution and emergency support.
